                            <comment id="16042176" author="githubbot" created="Thu, 8 Jun 2017 04:08:33 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user BruceXu1991 commented on the issue:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1908&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1908&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    This PR limit the output of paragraph in web, however it also limit the max download lines.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    My suggestion is to limit output of paragraph through zeppelin.interpreter.output.limit and limit the number of download lines through common.max_count.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16076605" author="robertmuil" created="Thu, 6 Jul 2017 14:32:37 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi all, is there a workaround for this? If Zeppelin does crash for a cell, and we cannot edit the underlying JSON, is there a way to recover?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16077411" author="thesuperzapper" created="Fri, 7 Jul 2017 00:33:20 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;You have to find some way to edit the JSON, and remove the output which is too long. (E.g. using VIM)&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16077558" author="moon" created="Fri, 7 Jul 2017 04:30:55 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Not sure if it helps, but if Zeppelin crashes because of output of a paragraph (cell), you can try click &quot;clear output&quot; on the main page, Next to the notebook title.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16077830" author="robertmuil" created="Fri, 7 Jul 2017 08:54:30 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thank you kindly! That&apos;s a great idea.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Much better than what I did: &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;start the notebook&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;click like a mad man to &apos;export script&apos; before it crashed&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;edit the script manually to remove offending output&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;reimport the script&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
